Alembic Database Migrations - Insight-Flow
==========================================

This directory contains database migration scripts for the Insight-Flow project.

QUICK START
-----------

Common Commands:

    # Create a new migration (auto-detect changes)
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add user preferences table"

    # Apply all pending migrations
    alembic upgrade head

    # Rollback one migration
    alembic downgrade -1

    # View migration history
    alembic history --verbose

    # Check current revision
    alembic current

    # Validate migrations
    python scripts/validate_migrations.py


BEST PRACTICES
--------------

1. USE SAFE MIGRATION HELPERS
   Always use functions from migration_helpers.py:
   - safe_add_column(), safe_drop_column()
   - safe_create_index(), safe_drop_index()
   - safe_create_table(), safe_drop_table()
   - safe_create_unique_constraint(), safe_drop_constraint()
   - safe_create_foreign_key()
   
2. ALWAYS TEST DOWNGRADE
   Every migration should have a working downgrade() function.

3. KEEP MIGRATIONS SMALL
   One logical change per migration.

4. NEVER EDIT APPLIED MIGRATIONS
   Create a new migration to fix issues instead.

5. AVOID SILENT EXCEPTION HANDLING
   Use safe_* helper functions instead of try/except with pass.

6. ADD MIGRATION DESCRIPTIONS
   Include a "Migration Description:" section in docstrings.


FILE NAMING CONVENTION
----------------------

New migrations will be created with date-prefixed format:

    YYYY_MM_DD_<revision_hash>_<slug>.py

Example: 2026_01_07_abc123de_add_user_settings.py

Note: Existing migrations may have different naming patterns
(hash-prefix, custom-prefix, or other). Do NOT rename existing 
migrations as this could cause version control issues. The 
revision chain uses revision IDs, not file names.


FILE STRUCTURE
--------------

alembic/
├── versions/           # Migration files
├── env.py              # Environment configuration  
├── script.py.mako      # Migration file template
└── README              # This file

alembic.ini             # Alembic configuration
migration_helpers.py    # Safe migration utilities
scripts/
└── validate_migrations.py  # Migration validation script


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------

"Target database is not up to date":
    alembic current
    alembic stamp <revision_id>

"Can't locate revision":
    alembic stamp head

"Multiple heads detected":
    alembic heads
    alembic merge heads -m "merge heads"

"Transaction aborted" error (asyncpg):
    Use safe_* functions from migration_helpers.py
    These functions check if objects exist before creating/dropping


For more information, see:
- https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/
- migration_helpers.py for safe utility functions